<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beaune</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beaune is a town in the Côte-d'Or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, at the heart of the Côte d'Or wine country between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dijon">Dijon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalon-sur-saone">Chalon-sur-Saône</a>. It was the seat of the ducal parlement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and is known for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hospices-de-beaune">Hospices de Beaune</a>, a hospital founded in 1443 by the chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicolas-rolin">Nicolas Rolin</a>. It is the main trading centre of Burgundy wine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beaune.jpg" alt="Beaune" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benjamin Smith · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beaune_-_H%C3%B4tel-Dieu_-_Cour_-_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
